<BaseLayout title="About XOCE" description="XOCE is Xef’s Open Computing Ecosystem. Meet the current Pebble projects, the principles behind the work and ways to contribute.">
  <main id="main" class="wrap section page-main"><header class="page-heading about-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Xef’s Open Computing Ecosystem</p><h1>Useful software.<br />Thoughtful details.</h1><p class="lead">XOCE is the home for Xef’s projects and their documentation. This website covers the Pebble watchface, apps and developer libraries available today.</p></header>
    <section class="about-intro"><div class="about-monogram" aria-hidden="true"><span>✳</span><strong>XOCE</strong><small>XEF’S OPEN COMPUTING ECOSYSTEM</small></div><div class="prose"><h2>The current collection.</h2><p><a href="/projects/dynamic/">Dynamic</a> displays the time, readings and ongoing activities. <a href="/projects/dashboard/">Dashboard</a> brings an activity, notifications and pinned items into one overview. <a href="/projects/timer/">Timer</a> manages countdowns on the watch, and <a href="/projects/open-activity/">Open Activity</a> connects Quick Launch to Dynamic’s displayed activities.</p><p>Two embedded libraries support developers: <a href="/projects/activities/">Activities</a> defines activity content and lifecycle, and <a href="/projects/core/">Core</a> provides shared readings and transport. Each of the six projects has its own repository and releases.</p><p>XOCE’s broader interests include Linux and KDE Plasma, Android, modern standards and new interaction ideas. The current collection documented here is for PebbleOS.</p></div></section>
    <section class="section about-principles"><p class="eyebrow">What guides the work</p><h2>Keep common tasks simple.</h2><div class="guide-grid"><article class="principle-card"><span class="principle-number">01</span><h3>Make it understandable.</h3><p>Use readable content, clear actions and useful feedback. Give people control over what they see.</p></article><article class="principle-card"><span class="principle-number">02</span><h3>Respect the device.</h3><p>Account for the screen, buttons, platform conventions and battery. Each app should work comfortably where it runs.</p></article><article class="principle-card"><span class="principle-number">03</span><h3>Be clear about state.</h3><p>Show current information, handle missing data and explain whether an action or saved change succeeded.</p></article></div><p class="image-caption"><a href="/design/">Read the design principles and current interface guidance.</a></p></section>
    <section class="contribute-panel" id="contribute"><div><p class="eyebrow">Get involved</p><h2>Help improve what is here.</h2><p>Try a development build, report a clear bug, improve a guide or build an activity provider. Share issues and code contributions in the affected project’s maintained repository.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button button-primary" href="/users/">Use the apps <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a><a class="button button-plain" href="/developers/">Developer resources <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div></div><div class="contribute-details"><Icon name="code" size={34}/><h3>Source and licences.</h3><p>The current Pebble projects publish their source under PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0. Project pages link to exact development releases, compatibility notes and their own licences.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/project/licensing/">Licensing & credits <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
